            <ArticleTitle>Angioplasty of pedicled right gastroepiploic artery graft through a six French diagnostic catheter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>638-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pedicled right gastroepiploic artery is increasingly being used as a conduit for coronary artery bypass surgery. We describe an interesting case in which balloon angioplasty for stenosis in such a graft was performed through a 6 French diagnostic catheter.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
